A 75-year-old man is brought to the emergency room 4 hours after the sudden onset of excruciating pain in his right calf. He has smoked 1 pack of cigarettes daily for 40 years. The right foot is cold and pale, and palpation of the right posterior tibial artery shows no pulse. Muscle strength is 1/5, and the sensation to touch significantly decreases in the right lower extremity. His serum creatinine kinase concentration is elevated. Arterial duplex sonography shows absent blood flow distal to the right popliteal artery. Compared with a healthy adult, which of the following sets of intracellular electrolyte concentrations are most likely to be found in this patient&#39;s right distal gastrocnemius muscle?
			Na+
			K+
			Ca2+
